--- Ada's diary ---
I waited at Mr. Hale's office this morning, from nine to a quarter past nine, and spoke to Arthur, and then went on to Finsbury Circus.

--- Arthur's diary ---
I went to the clerks' room of the Moorgate Fire and Life Assurance Company, on the third floor, this morning, and spoke to Thomas. I also bought a paper. Thomas and I have been fellow-clerks for five years, and, although we never quarrel, we see little of each other, except during business hours. I went to the news-stand at Moorgate Underground station, and bought another paper, and then returned to the clerks' room.

